      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The as-cast AlCoCrFeNi2.1 alloy exhibits high strength and ductility at room temperature.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC4145285::hypothesis_evidence_v2::23f62f72fb141399",
        "PMC9955357::hypothesis_evidence_v2::57d3b8ea889bc367"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Intermediate thermal aging produces a transient ductile-brittle-ductile transition in eutectic FCC/B2 high-entropy alloys.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The transient embrittlement is driven by evolution of local chemical order within B2 domains and associated changes in phase-boundary morphology.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed transition is not caused by grain-boundary embrittlement.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Aging forms coherent ordered L12-type precipitates within the B2 phase.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Aging enhances B2 ordering within the B2 phase.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Aging changes the coherency or morphology of FCC/B2 phase boundaries.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Strong local chemical order in B2 domains impedes dislocation cross-slip.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Restricted cross-slip promotes planar slip localization.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Planar slip localization causes brittle fracture.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At higher aging temperatures, thermal activation enables increased dislocation cross-slip.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Higher aging temperatures promote annihilation of stacking faults.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Thermally activated cross-slip and stacking-fault annihilation restore ductility.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "For AlCoCrFeNi2.1, the embrittlement regime lies between approximately 400°C and 600°C.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "AlCoCrFeNi2.1 recovers ductility above approximately 600°C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Outside the 400–600°C embrittlement range, the alloy remains ductile.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Embrittlement is characterized by a sharp decrease in elongation and a transition from ductile to brittle fracture.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "If local chemical order and phase-boundary morphology control embrittlement, in-situ TEM should show planar slip and limited cross-slip within ordered domains.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "If grain-boundary embrittlement controls failure, dislocations should pile up at grain boundaries and fracture should initiate at those boundaries.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment",
